# XBD 7.2 POSIX Locale
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The POSIX locale is observed only through its behaviour for the portable
# characters and the langinfo and localeconv values the tables of XBD 7.3
# give. creating locales is optional (POSIX2_LOCALEDEF): these tests report
# NOTINUSE when the system does not claim it.

assertion  XBD.7.2-posix-locale.001
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.2
class      required
since      1992
says       The C locale and the POSIX locale are identical: classes, case
           mappings, collation, langinfo items, localeconv() and the code
           set agree.
test       t/001-c-and-posix-identical.c

assertion  XBD.7.2-posix-locale.002
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.2
class      required
since      1992
says       A locale built with localedef from the POSIX locale tables
           answers like the POSIX locale for classes, case maps, collation,
           langinfo items and localeconv().
timeout    120
test       t/002-as-if-localedef-tables.c

assertion  XBD.7.2-posix-locale.003
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.2
class      required
since      1992
says       When no locale environment variable is set, or all are empty,
           selecting the locale from the environment succeeds and leaves a
           locale in which the portable characters work.
test       t/003-default-locale-exists.c
